---
// The pages the Sessions card opens (switch UX round 2), in place of the profile's settings like the Switch page:
// Restore (a preview, then steps, then checks, and an undo of its own; or "Not yet" while a switch is unfinished),
// Export and Import. settings.astro shows them and fills in the profile's name ([data-pn]) and the backup's name
// ([data-bk-name]). Sample figures only; nothing on this Mac changes.
---
<div class="sess-pages" data-sess-pages hidden>
  <!-- Restore… -->
  <section class="sw-page" data-sp="restore">
    <div class="sw-head"><h3 data-rs-head>Restore <span data-pn>work</span> from “<span data-bk-name></span>”</h3></div>
    <div class="sw-run" data-rs="preview"><span class="disp"><em>Preview · nothing written yet · nothing is ever overwritten</em></span></div>
    <div class="sw-run" data-rs="run"><span class="disp"><span class="b">Restoring ●</span> <em>· step 2 of 3 · <span data-rs-count>14</span> of 26 back</em></span><span class="spacer"></span><button type="button" class="pill small tint t-red" data-rs-stop>Stop, keep what's back</button></div>
    <div class="sw-run" data-rs="done"><span class="disp"><span class="g">Restored</span> <em>· 26 back · nothing overwritten · 3 listed</em></span><span class="spacer"></span><button type="button" class="key k" data-rs-undo>Undo this restore</button><button type="button" class="key k" data-sess-back>Back to <span data-pn>work</span>'s settings</button></div>
    <div class="sw-run" data-rs="refused"><span class="disp"><span class="a">Not yet</span> <em>· one thing first · nothing written</em></span></div>
    <div class="sw-cols">
      <div class="sw-col">
        <div class="card"><h4>What happens <i class="idot" title="What the restore will do with each thing in the backup, worked out before anything is written. It merges and never overwrites.">i</i></h4>
          <div class="srow"><span>Back where it was</span><span class="v-soft"><b>10</b> entries the switch moved, unchanged since</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Missing, restored</span><span class="v-soft"><b>4</b> entries · <b>12</b> transcripts</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Made after the backup</span><span class="v-soft"><b>6</b> sessions: kept</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Changed since</span><span class="v-soft"><b>3</b>: left as they are now, listed</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>In use</span><span class="v-soft"><b>1</b> transcript a running Claude Code session holds: left alone, listed</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Would be deleted <i class="idot" title="Claude Code deletes the transcript of a session once it is older than cleanupPeriodDays (~/.claude/settings.json, 30 by default). A transcript comes back with its real age, so one older than that would be deleted again. Sessions started or last continued in the Claude window aren't counted: Claude Code keeps them at any age (2.1.248 and later), unless you deleted or archived the session in the Claude window (an archived one goes after a grace period). Your organisation's managed settings (or an error in them), HIPAA and zero data retention make the period apply to all of them; cl_audit can't see HIPAA or zero data retention. A project's own .claude/settings.json can also set a shorter period, which cl_audit can't see.">i</i></span><span class="v-soft"><b>9</b>: Claude Code would delete them again. Keep for 90 days would save all of them. <button type="button" class="key k" data-sess-keep>Keep for 90 days</button></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="card"><h4>Stays as it is <i class="idot" title="Restore only adds what is missing. The account, the sign-ins and claude.ai are not part of it; a file that is here (MCP settings, settings.json, a task file) is never replaced or merged into.">i</i></h4>
          <div class="srow"><span>Account</span><span class="v-soft">The profile stays on the account it's on: a switch changes that</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Sign-ins</span><span class="v-soft">Never in a backup, never written</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>MCP</span><span class="v-soft">Not in this Mac's backups: the window's MCP settings travel only in the encrypted export. Yours stay as they are</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>settings.json</span><span class="v-soft">Yours stay; one is added only if none is here and you pick Add them</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Scheduled tasks</span><span class="v-soft">A task file that is there stays as it is; only a missing one comes back</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>claude.ai</span><span class="v-soft">Chats and Projects</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sw-col">
        <div class="card" data-rs="preview"><h4>Steps <i class="idot" title="What restoring does, in order, each step checked before the next. A receipt is kept as it goes, so if the Mac stops, the next start finishes it first.">i</i></h4>
          <ol class="sw-steps">
            <li><i></i><div><b><span data-pn>work</span>'s Claude window closes</b><span>Only that window, about half a minute.</span></div></li>
            <li><i></i><div><b>What's listed comes back</b><span>Merged by the rules in What happens; nothing overwritten.</span></div></li>
            <li><i></i><div><b>The window opens; the sidebar, as before</b><span>Press Return in the session that opens.</span></div></li>
          </ol>
          <div class="sw-keys"><button type="button" class="key k" data-sess-back>Cancel</button><span></span><button type="button" class="pill small tint t-green" data-rs-go>Close and restore 26</button></div>
        </div>
        <div class="card" data-rs="run"><h4>Steps</h4>
          <ol class="sw-steps">
            <li class="done"><i></i><div><b><span data-pn>work</span>'s Claude window closed</b></div></li>
            <li class="now"><i></i><div><b>What's listed comes back</b><div class="chk"><span class="disp"><em><span data-rs-count>14</span> of 26 · nothing overwritten</em></span></div></div></li>
            <li><i></i><div><b>The window opens; the sidebar, as before</b></div></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="g-note sub">It keeps a receipt as it goes, like a switch: if the Mac stops, the next start finishes it first.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card" data-rs="done"><h4>Steps</h4>
          <ol class="sw-steps">
            <li class="done"><i></i><div><b><span data-pn>work</span>'s Claude window</b><div class="chk"><span class="disp"><span class="g">Open again ✓</span></span></div></div></li>
            <li class="done"><i></i><div><b>What's listed came back</b><div class="chk"><span class="disp"><span class="g">26 back · 0 overwritten ✓</span></span></div><span>3 changed since stayed as they were.</span></div></li>
            <li class="warn"><i></i><div><b>The sidebar, as before</b><div class="chk"><span class="disp"><em>Press Return in “cl_audit · arrange sidebar”</em></span></div></div></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="g-note sub">Undo this restore takes back exactly what it put back.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card" data-rs="refused"><h4>First</h4>
          <ol class="sw-steps">
            <li class="warn"><i></i><div><b>A switch of <span data-pn>work</span> is unfinished</b><span>It stopped half way. Undo it first: its receipt puts back exactly what it moved, then restore if anything's still missing.</span></div></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="g-note sub">One switch, restore or import at a time.</p>
          <div class="sw-keys"><button type="button" class="key k" data-sess-back>Back</button><span></span><button type="button" class="pill small tint t-green dimmed">Close and restore 26</button></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Export… -->
  <section class="sw-page" data-sp="export">
    <div class="sw-head"><h3>Export <span data-pn>work</span>'s sessions</h3></div>
    <div class="sw-run"><span class="disp"><em>Preview · nothing written yet</em></span><span class="spacer"></span><button type="button" class="pill small" data-sess-go="move">Move to another Mac</button></div>
    <div class="sw-cols">
      <div class="sw-col">
        <div class="card"><h4>What <i class="idot" title="Which sessions go in the file.">i</i></h4>
          <div class="srow"><span>From</span><select class="menu" aria-label="From"><option>This profile, as it is now</option><option>One of its backups</option><option>All profiles</option></select></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Claude Code</span><span class="v-soft">310 sessions, with their sub-agent files</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Claude window</span><span class="v-soft">17 Code-tab entries, 2 tasks</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="card"><h4>Keys found <i class="idot" title="Sessions can hold keys pasted into them. They stay out of the file unless it gets a password.">i</i></h4>
          <div class="srow"><span>Found</span><span class="v-soft"><b>5</b> sessions hold keys: 2 GitHub tokens, 3 private keys</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Those 5</span><select class="menu" aria-label="Sessions with keys"><option>Leave them out</option><option>Keep them: needs a password</option></select></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sw-col">
        <div class="card"><h4>Preview</h4>
          <div class="srow"><span>~/projects/app</span><span class="v-soft"><b>210</b> · 3.9 GB</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>~/projects/site</span><span class="v-soft"><b>95</b> · 1.6 GB</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>~/projects/infra</span><span class="v-soft"><b>5</b> with keys: left out</span></div>
          <p class="g-note sub">One file that Finder opens, never with a sign-in. Accounts cl_audit knows appear only as a fingerprint; an address typed into a conversation stays as written.</p>
          <div class="sw-keys"><button type="button" class="key k" data-sess-back>Cancel</button><span></span><button type="button" class="pill small tint t-green" data-sess-demo="Export">Export 305 sessions · ≈ 5.5 GB</button></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Import… -->
  <section class="sw-page" data-sp="import">
    <div class="sw-head"><h3>Import into <span data-pn>work</span></h3></div>
    <div class="sw-run"><span class="disp"><em>Preview · nothing written yet · nothing is ever overwritten</em></span></div>
    <div class="sw-cols">
      <div class="sw-col">
        <div class="card"><h4>From <i class="idot" title="The file you picked, and the profile it goes into.">i</i></h4>
          <div class="srow"><span>File</span><select class="menu" aria-label="File" data-sess-file><option value="import" selected>an export made on another Mac</option><option value="import-move">a move from another Mac</option></select></div>
          <p class="g-note sub">The file is unpacked as a backup of <span data-pn>work</span> first, then restored from: the same rules as Restore.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sw-col">
        <div class="card"><h4>What happens</h4>
          <div class="srow"><span>New</span><span class="v-soft"><b>210</b>: added</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Already here</span><span class="v-soft"><b>60</b> with the same content: skipped</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Grown on both sides</span><span class="v-soft"><b>3</b>: this profile's copy stays, listed</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Code-tab entries</span><span class="v-soft"><b>10</b>: the window closes and opens again</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Folder not here</span><span class="v-soft"><b>30</b>: added, shown once that folder exists</span></div>
          <div class="sw-keys"><button type="button" class="key k" data-sess-back>Cancel</button><span></span><button type="button" class="pill small tint t-green" data-sess-demo="Import">Close and import 210 sessions</button></div>
          <p class="g-note sub">Afterwards, Undo last import (under the profile's Sessions) removes exactly what it added.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Export ▸ Move to another Mac (26.11.10): one key sets all profiles, the encrypted disk image, the setup, the
       window's MCP settings and tasks, and cl_audit's own profiles. Sample names only (the demo's home, work, side). -->
  <section class="sw-page" data-sp="move">
    <div class="sw-head"><h3>Move to another Mac</h3></div>
    <div class="sw-run"><span class="disp"><em>Preview · nothing written yet</em></span></div>
    <div class="sw-cols">
      <div class="sw-col">
        <div class="card"><h4>What <i class="idot" title="Which sessions go in the file.">i</i></h4>
          <div class="srow"><span>From</span><select class="menu" aria-label="From"><option>This profile, as it is now</option><option>One of its backups</option><option selected>All profiles</option></select></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>Move <i class="idot" title="Move to another Mac: everything a new Mac needs in one encrypted disk image: every profile's sessions, Claude Code's setup, the window's MCP settings and scheduled tasks, and cl_audit's own profiles and settings. A move keeps the real account ids and addresses (no fingerprints), because the Claude window files its Code-tab list and scheduled tasks by account: the new Mac puts them back where the window looks once you sign in there. That is why a move is only ever the encrypted image. Sign-ins never travel: you sign in to each account on the new Mac.">i</i></span><span class="v-soft">On: your accounts keep their real identifiers and email addresses, so the new Mac can put each Code-tab entry and scheduled task back under the right account. That is why a move is always a password-protected disk image, never a plain zip.<small class="ap-note">Sign-ins don't travel. On the new Mac you sign in again to each account (Add account).</small></span></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>Claude Code</span><span class="v-soft">610 sessions, with their sub-agent files · 9.8 GB</span></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>Claude window</span><span class="v-soft">41 Code-tab entries, 4 scheduled tasks<small class="ap-note">4 scheduled tasks with their prompts. An import adds them only if you pick Add them, and they come paused.</small></span></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>MCP settings</span><span class="v-soft">3 MCP servers (github, postgres, browser) and the window's other settings: in the encrypted disk image</span></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>Claude Code setup</span><span class="v-soft">CLAUDE.md with 2 included files, 23 skills, 4 agents, 6 commands, 1 output style, keybindings, settings.json with 4 hooks and a status line, 3 scripts, 2 plugins to reinstall</span></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>cl_audit's profiles</span><span class="v-soft">3 profiles (home, work, side): accounts, looks, Dock places, and cl_audit's General and backup settings. Carried in the encrypted disk image only.</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Cowork</span><span class="v-soft">left out</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sw-col">
        <div class="card"><h4>Keys found <i class="idot" title="Sessions can hold keys pasted into them. They stay out of the file unless you keep them.">i</i></h4>
          <div class="srow"><span>Found</span><span class="v-soft"><b>5</b> sessions hold keys: 2 GitHub tokens, 3 private keys</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Those 5</span><select class="menu" aria-label="Sessions with keys"><option>Leave them out</option><option>Keep them: needs a password</option></select></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>Password</span><span class="v-soft">An encrypted disk image<small class="ap-note">Not stored anywhere. Lose it and the file can't be opened.</small></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="card"><h4>Preview</h4>
          <div class="srow"><span>home</span><span class="v-soft"><b>310</b> · 5.6 GB</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>work</span><span class="v-soft"><b>240</b> · 3.4 GB</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>side</span><span class="v-soft"><b>60</b> · 0.8 GB · <b>5</b> with keys: left out</span></div>
          <p class="g-note sub">Close each profile's Claude window first, or its Code-tab list is left out.</p>
          <div class="sw-keys"><button type="button" class="key k" data-sess-back>Cancel</button><span></span><button type="button" class="pill small tint t-green" data-sess-demo="Move">Export 605 sessions · ≈ 9.7 GB</button></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Import… of a move file (26.11.10): cl_audit's profiles first (Make 2 profiles), then Close and import; the done
       state lists what's next for each made profile. data-mv = plan | done. -->
  <section class="sw-page" data-sp="import-move">
    <div class="sw-head"><h3>Import into home</h3></div>
    <div class="sw-run"><span class="disp"><em>Preview · a move from another Mac · nothing is ever overwritten</em></span></div>
    <div class="sw-cols">
      <div class="sw-col">
        <div class="card"><h4>From <i class="idot" title="The file you picked, and the profile it goes into.">i</i></h4>
          <div class="srow"><span>File</span><select class="menu" aria-label="File" data-sess-file><option value="import">an export made on another Mac</option><option value="import-move" selected>a move from another Mac</option></select></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Profile in the file</span><span class="v-soft">home</span></div>
          <p class="g-note sub">On the new Mac, home is the first profile (<code>~/.claude</code>), set up by cl_audit's first run.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card"><h4>cl_audit's profiles <i class="idot" title="The file holds cl_audit's own record of its profiles (name, look, Dock place, accounts and the one in use) and its General and backup settings. Import makes the profiles that aren't here and never changes one that is. A made profile works in folders of its own, whatever the file says. It is made with its accounts, looks and settings, but not signed in: after the import, sign in to each account with Add account. No Dock icon yet: you put it in the Dock after the import. Your settings stay unless you take the file's. Take back the profiles it made undoes exactly what was made.">i</i></h4>
          <p class="g-note sub">A move from another Mac: the file keeps the real accounts, so the entries and tasks go back under them.</p>
          <div data-mv="plan">
            <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>Profiles</span><span class="v-soft">2 to make: work (3 accounts), side (1 account) · here already: home<small class="ap-note">Made with their accounts, looks and settings, but not signed in: after the import, sign in to each account with Add account. No Dock icon yet: you put it in the Dock after the import. Each works in folders of its own, whatever the file says.</small></span></div>
            <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>Settings</span><span class="v-soft">2 differ (Face, Keep the last): this Mac's stay<small class="ap-note">Face: Std here, Silver in the file</small><small class="ap-note">Keep the last: 3 here, 5 in the file</small></span></div>
            <div class="sw-keys"><span></span><span></span><button type="button" class="pill small tint t-green" data-mv-make>Make 2 profiles</button></div>
            <p class="g-note sub">Do this first. Then the page offers the part's own profile for Into, and Close and import puts its sessions there.</p>
          </div>
          <div data-mv="done">
            <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>Done</span><span class="v-soft">Made: work, side<small class="ap-note">They aren't signed in and have no Dock icon yet: what to do next for each is listed below.</small></span></div>
            <div class="sw-keys"><span></span><span></span><button type="button" class="key k" data-mv-undo>Take back the profiles it made</button></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sw-col">
        <div class="card"><h4>What happens</h4>
          <div class="srow"><span>Into</span><span class="v-soft">home: the part's own profile</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>New</span><span class="v-soft"><b>310</b>: added</span></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>Code-tab entries</span><span class="v-soft"><b>17</b>: each back in the folder of its own account, shown once you sign in there</span></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>Scheduled tasks</span><span class="v-soft"><b>2</b>: only if you pick Add them, and they come paused</span></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>Setup and MCP settings</span><span class="v-soft">Only if you pick Add them; added only where none is here</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>Folder not here</span><span class="v-soft"><b>30</b>: added, shown once that folder exists</span></div>
          <div class="sw-keys"><button type="button" class="key k" data-sess-back>Cancel</button><span></span><button type="button" class="pill small tint t-green" data-sess-demo="Import a move" data-mv-go>Close and import 310 sessions</button></div>
          <p class="g-note sub" data-mv="plan">Close and import waits until the profiles are made.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card" data-mv="done"><h4>On this Mac, next</h4>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>work</span><span class="v-soft">Sign in to each of its 3 accounts (team-1@work.example, team-2@work.example, team-3@work.example): Settings ▸ work ▸ Claude Code ▸ Accounts ▸ Add account. Nothing is signed in yet.<small class="ap-note">Put it in the Dock: Settings ▸ work ▸ Dock icon ▸ Usage in the Dock, or the key here. It had a Dock icon on the other Mac.</small><small class="ap-note">Its sessions: Settings ▸ work ▸ Sessions ▸ Import…, the same file. Into is work there, and Profile in the file shows work's part.</small></span></div>
          <div class="sw-keys"><span></span><span></span><button type="button" class="key k" data-mv-dock="work">Put work in the Dock</button></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>side</span><span class="v-soft">Sign in to its account (side@example.com): Settings ▸ side ▸ Claude Code ▸ Accounts ▸ Add account. Nothing is signed in yet.<small class="ap-note">Put it in the Dock: Settings ▸ side ▸ Dock icon ▸ Usage in the Dock, or the key here. It had a Dock icon on the other Mac.</small><small class="ap-note">Its sessions: Settings ▸ side ▸ Sessions ▸ Import…, the same file. Into is side there, and Profile in the file shows side's part.</small></span></div>
          <div class="sw-keys"><span></span><span></span><button type="button" class="key k" data-mv-dock="side">Put side in the Dock</button></div>
        </div>
        <div class="card"><h4>Stays as it is <i class="idot" title="Import only adds what is missing. The account, the sign-ins and claude.ai are not part of it; a file that is here (MCP settings, settings.json, a task file) is never replaced or merged into.">i</i></h4>
          <div class="srow"><span>Sign-ins</span><span class="v-soft">Never travel: sign in again on this Mac</span></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>MCP</span><span class="v-soft">Yours stay; the file's are added only if none is here and you pick Add them</span></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>settings.json</span><span class="v-soft">Yours stay; one is added only if none is here and you pick Add them</span></div>
          <div class="srow vcol stk"><span>Scheduled tasks</span><span class="v-soft">A task file that is here stays as it is; the file's tasks come only if you picked Add them, paused</span></div>
          <div class="srow"><span>claude.ai</span><span class="v-soft">Chats and Projects</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
